-- title:
--   Reducedness of A/(p) descends from B/pB
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be commutative rings with $B$ an $A$-algebra, and suppose the structure map $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A\ B$ is injective. Fix an element $p \in A$ and assume, as an instance hypothesis, that the quotient ring $B/(\,\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A\ B\ p\,)$ by the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$ is reduced. Let $S \subseteq A$ be a subset subject to two conditions: first, every $b \in B$ admits some $s \in S$ and some $a \in A$ with $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A\ B\ a = (\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A\ B\ s)\cdot b$ in $B$, i.e. $b$ becomes an element of the image of $A$ after multiplication by an element of $S$; second, for every $s \in S$ and every $a \in A$, membership $s\,a \in (p)$ forces $a \in (p)$, i.e. $A/(p)$ has no $S$-torsion. The conclusion is that the quotient $A/(p)$ by the principal ideal generated by $p$ is reduced.
--
--   An elementary descent step: reducedness of the special fibre is checked over a ring $B$ in which $p$ remains well behaved and then transferred back to $A$, provided the passage from $B$ to $A$ is controlled by multipliers $S$ that act injectively on $A/(p)$. It is used in the proof of [`IsIntegrallyClosed.isReduced_quotient_span_singleton_of_squarefree_minpoly`](thm.html#IsIntegrallyClosed.isReduced_quotient_span_singleton_of_squarefree_minpoly), where $B$ is a ring generated by an integral element whose minimal polynomial is squarefree modulo $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsReduced_quotient_span_singleton_of_injective_of_forall_exists_mul_mem.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem IsReduced.quotient_span_singleton_of_injective_of_forall_exists_mul_mem
    {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B)) (p : A)
    [IsReduced (B ⧸ Ideal.span {algebraMap A B p})]
    (S : Set A)
    (hS : ∀ b : B, ∃ s ∈ S, ∃ a : A, algebraMap A B a = algebraMap A B s * b)
    (htf : ∀ s ∈ S, ∀ a : A, s * a ∈ Ideal.span {p} → a ∈ Ideal.span {p}) :
    IsReduced (A ⧸ Ideal.span {p}) := by sorry
